# SQL Setup Scripts

IMPORTANT: This directory is not the live-upgrade mechanism for an already
deployed production database.

The supported boundary is:
- use this SQL bootstrap chain for local/dev rebuilds, tests, and the one-time
  initial deployment bootstrap from a `003`-contract dump
- establish Alembic ownership immediately after that bootstrap
- use Alembic migrations for every live schema change after production exists

## Purpose

These SQL files are designed to:
1. Set up a fresh development database quickly
2. Provide a reference for the complete database schema
3. Import synthetic test data for development

## Seed Data Contract

`003-import-data.sql` is a compact synthetic seed committed in this repository.
It intentionally captures representative data complexity (null/non-null states,
active/inactive entities, schedule/log variability) without historical volume.

`900-import-new-data.sql` then maps `user-dept.csv`, `dev-dept.csv`, and
`devperm.csv` into the auth model.

Route tests enforce this contract in
`tests/unit/test_seed_shape_contract.py` (under the `route` marker). If you
change seed files, keep that test green or update it with an explicit rationale.

## Usage

To set up a development database:

```bash
# Start fresh (drops existing database)
DROP_DB=true bash 000-init.sh

# Try to run migrations on existing database
bash 000-init.sh
```

## Important Notes

1. **Not A Live Upgrade Tool**: These scripts are not the supported mechanism
   for upgrading an already deployed production database. Use Alembic for live
   post-deployment schema changes.

2. **Schema Management**:
   - The canonical schema is defined in SQLAlchemy models
   - These SQL files are derived from those models
   - Always update the models first, then regenerate these files
   - For live database changes, use Alembic migrations

## File Structure

- `000-init.sh`: Main setup script
- `001-schema.sql`: Base schema definition
- `[000-999]-*.sql`: Ordered migration files
- `*.sample.sql`: Example data files

## Additional Tools

- `generate-schemapdf.sh`: Creates a PDF of the ER diagram from schema.er
  (Requires the 'erd' tool to be installed)

For the supported initial-deployment rehearsal/bootstrap path, use
`pixi run rehearse-initial-deployment`. For live production schema changes,
refer to the Alembic migration documentation in `scheduler/alembic/`.

N.B. the database schema should be managed by Alembic to support schema
migrations of a live database. Currently the SQLAlchemy models fully capture the
schema represented by the files in this directory.

This directory contains the schema for the scheduler.. It is primarily intended
for reproduction of a development database not schema migrations of a live
database. It will only work for building the new database out of the old
database.

The generate-schemapdf.sh command turns schema.er into a pdf of a simplified ER diagram using the erd tool. If it is not installed the script will not run.
